{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793436912,"nonce":"pEoEK/UxSZl71PxO5V3a8V1We2g=","title":"CI: skip PR workflows by label (stacked PRs, Actions minutes)","message":"Actions minutes are limited, and stacked PRs (a 5-10 PR stack such as ADR-0076's) each run the full CI on every push, though only the stack tip's run matters.\n\nProposal:\n- A PR label, e.g. `ci:skip`, makes the PR-triggered jobs skip: ci.yml (test-and-coverage, ui-tests, openapi-drift, the ui job), kind.yml, and image.yml's pull_request build. Add `labeled`/`unlabeled` to the `pull_request` types (with opened/synchronize/reopened) so removing the label starts a run; gate each job with `if: !contains(github.event.pull_request.labels.*.name, 'ci:skip')` (cheapest: in the existing `changes` job of ci.yml so dependent jobs skip without starting runners).\n- Optionally `ci:skip-kind` / `ci:skip-image` for finer control, and `ci:full` to force everything.\n- push to main and v* tags never skip.\n- `just pr-gate \u003cn\u003e` (scripts/pr_gate.py, .github/required-checks.txt) must treat a skipped run as NOT passing: a PR labelled ci:skip cannot pass the gate until the label is removed and CI runs on its head. Merge order for a stack: remove the label from the bottom PR, let it run, merge, repeat (or run once on the tip and merge down).\n- Note: concurrency in ci.yml already cancels superseded runs per ref (cancel-in-progress) — keep it.\n- Document the labels in CONTRIBUTING or the PR template.\n\nAcceptance: a PR with ci:skip shows the jobs as skipped and uses no runner minutes beyond the tiny label-check; removing the label triggers a full run; pr-gate refuses a PR whose last head SHA has no passing required checks.","files":null}]}